.TH COFF_STORAGE_CLASS 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
coff_storage_class \- Retrieve the storage class name for a COFF symbol

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/coff.h>

.IB const char*
.IB coff_storage_class (uint8 sclass);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcoff_storage_class\fR function is used to retrieve the storage class name for a COFF symbol. It takes a storage class value \fBsclass\fR as a parameter. The function returns a pointer to a string representing the storage class name.

.SH coff_storage_class
The \fBcoff_storage_class\fR function retrieves the storage class name for a COFF symbol. It takes a storage class value \fBsclass\fR as a parameter. The function returns a pointer to a string representing the storage class name.

The function returns a pointer to a string representing the storage class name, or \fBNULL\fR if the storage class value is not recognized.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcoff_storage_class\fR function to retrieve the storage class name for a COFF symbol:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/coff.h>

int main() {
    uint8 storage_class = COFF_C_EXT;
    const char* class_name = coff_storage_class(storage_class);

    if(class_name != NULL) {
        // Use the storage class name

        printf("Storage class: %s\n", class_name);
    } else {
        printf("Unknown storage class\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
.nef